# Paperclip × Hermes Agent — SWOT, Diagnosis & Strategy

## 🔍 Root Cause Diagnosis: Why Your Adapters Are Failing

After analyzing your codebase, I found **three clear root causes** for your adapter failures:

### Root Cause #1: Your agents are running on free/weak models

Your `.paperclip.yaml` shows **all 11 agents** in Idea Factory use cheap or free models:

| Agent | Model | Problem |
|-------|-------|---------|
| ceo-agent | `anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet` | ✅ Good model, but older version |
| yc-scout | `google/gemini-2.5-flash` | ⚠️ Cheap, weak at multi-step planning |
| trend-mapper | `deepseek/deepseek-r1:free` | 🔴 **Free tier = aggressive rate limits, no function calling** |
| idea-scorer | `deepseek/deepseek-r1:free` | 🔴 Same — free models often skip/ignore tools |
| kill-switch | `google/gemini-2.5-flash` | ⚠️ Flash is fast but poor at complex reasoning |
| product-architect | `deepseek/deepseek-r1:free` | 🔴 Free tier — unreliable for tool use |
| cto-agent | `qwen/qwen-2.5-coder-32b-instruct:free` | 🔴 **Free tier, poor function calling support** |
| coder-agent | `qwen/qwen-2.5-coder-32b-instruct:free` | 🔴 Same issues |
| designer-agent | `meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free` | 🔴 **Llama 3.3 has limited function calling** |
| landing-page-agent | `qwen/qwen-2.5-coder-32b-instruct:free` | 🔴 Same issues |
| growth-agent | `google/gemini-2.5-flash` | ⚠️ Too weak for strategic planning |

> [!CAUTION]
> **7 out of 11 agents use `:free` models.** Free-tier models on OpenRouter have:
> - Aggressive rate limiting (429 errors = "ultra mode errors")
> - Poor or no native function-calling support
> - Lower quality responses
> - Higher latency and frequent timeouts
>
> **This is almost certainly your main problem.** Hermes won't fix this — it would hit the same model quality issues.

### Root Cause #2: Windows compatibility

Your tool executor uses `run_bash_command` which calls `exec(command)` — this runs in the **system shell**. On Windows, that's `cmd.exe`, not `bash`. So any bash-specific commands (grep, ls, cat, etc.) will fail unless you have WSL/Git Bash in your PATH.

### Root Cause #3: Prompt-mode fallback limitations

Paperclip's agentic loop *does* have a smart fallback for models without native function calling (it injects `<tool_call>` XML into the prompt). But free-tier models often:
- Ignore the tool instructions entirely
- Generate malformed JSON inside `<tool_call>` blocks
- Just describe what they would do instead of actually calling tools

